## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of user-space vs kernel-space concept interplay, synchronization primitives, and designing a lazy I/O cache with proper wakeups.

## Key Concepts

- Per-block state machine (EMPTY, PENDING, LOADED, ERROR)
- Fast path vs slow path with contention handling
- Wait queues (futex/condvar) and wakeup semantics
- Avoiding thundering herd with CAS and double-checked locking
- Error propagation from I/O to callers

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct {
  void *data;
  atomic_int state; // 0=EMPTY,1=PENDING,2=LOADED,3=ERROR
  int waiters;
  pthread_mutex_t mutex;
  pthread_cond_t cond;
} cache_entry;

#define EMPTY 0
#define PENDING 1
#define LOADED 2
#define ERROR 3

void* block_read(int block_id) {
  cache_entry *entry = &cache[block_id];

  // Fast path
  if (atomic_load(&entry->state) == LOADED) {
    return entry->data;
  }

  pthread_mutex_lock(&entry->mutex);

  // Double-check after acquiring lock
  if (atomic_load(&entry->state) == LOADED) {
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&entry->mutex);
    return entry->data;
  }

  // Transition to PENDING if first thread
  if (atomic_compare_exchange_strong(&entry->state, &EMPTY, PENDING)) {
    enqueue_io_request(block_id);
  }

  // Block until I/O completes
  while (atomic_load(&entry->state) == PENDING) {
    entry->waiters++;
    pthread_cond_wait(&entry->cond, &entry->mutex);
    entry->waiters--;
  }

  pthread_mutex_unlock(&entry->mutex);

  if (atomic_load(&entry->state) == ERROR) {
    return NULL; // Propagate error
  }

  return entry->data;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of synchronization primitives and memory ordering in a toy OS context.

## Key Concepts

- Barrier reuse via a generation counter
- Race-free wakeups with a condition variable analogue
- Memory visibility and minimal locking
- Testing for progress and fairness under contention

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct {
  int count;
  int needed;
  int gen;
  pthread_mutex_t m;
  pthread_cond_t cv;
} barrier_t;

void barrier_init(barrier_t *b, int n) {
  b->count = 0;
  b->needed = n;
  b->gen = 0;
  pthread_mutex_init(&b->m, NULL);
  pthread_cond_init(&b->cv, NULL);
}

void barrier_wait(barrier_t *b) {
  pthread_mutex_lock(&b->m);
  int g = b->gen;
  if (++b->count == b->needed) {
    b->count = 0;
    b->gen++;
    pthread_cond_broadcast(&b->cv);
  } else {
    while (b->gen == g) {
      pthread_cond_wait(&b->cv, &b->m);
    }
  }
  pthread_mutex_unlock(&b->m);
}
```

